-- title:
--   Relative norm of the content of a principal idèle
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with a $K$-algebra structure on $L$, and let $\beta \in L^{\times}$. Form the diagonal (principal) idèle of $\beta$, i.e. the image of $\beta$ under the map of unit groups induced by $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$, project it to the unit group of the finite adèle ring of $\mathcal{O}_L$ in $L$ via `projFin`, and take its content `fadContentHom L`, namely the invertible fractional ideal $\prod_{w} \mathfrak{q}_w^{-\log \lvert \cdot \rvert_w}$ formed as the multipliable product over the height-one primes $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ of the fractional ideal generated by $w$ raised to the exponent $-\log$ of the valuation of the $w$-component. The assertion is that applying `fracRelNormUnit K L` to this unit — the homomorphism on invertible fractional ideals which sends a prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$, with multiplicity, to the fractional ideal of the prime $\mathfrak{p} = w \cap \mathcal{O}_K$ lying under $w$ raised to the inertia degree $f(w \mid \mathfrak{p})$ — gives exactly the content of the principal idèle of the field norm $N_{L/K}(\beta) \in K^{\times}$, obtained by transporting $\beta$ along `Algebra.norm K` as a monoid homomorphism $L^{\times} \to K^{\times}$ and then repeating the diagonal–project–content construction over $K$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the relative ideal norm with the field norm on principal ideals, $N_{L/K}(\beta\mathcal{O}_L) = N_{L/K}(\beta)\mathcal{O}_K$, stated with both sides written as contents of principal idèles. It feeds the identification of the quotient of the idèle class group by the subgroup generated by norms and by principal idèles with a ray class group in `exists_mulEquiv_quotient_normRaySubgroup_apply_eq_contents_of_anchors`.
